  "content": "When combining the words 'I am' and 'getting' you are telling someone 'you' are gaining possession, being affected by or have plans to seek out and obtain a particular thing.\nHere are some examples:\n\"I'm getting better.\"\n\"I'm getting ready for bed.\"\n\"I'm getting a tooth ache.\"\n\"I'm getting a cold.\"\n\"I'm getting married.\"\n\"I'm getting tired.\"\n\"I'm getting good at reading.\"\n\"I'm getting a new car.\"\n\"I'm getting a job.\"\n\"I'm getting a puppy.\"",
